    "result_text": "All 274 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe specification required storing telephone numbers as digits-only and normalizing before the uniqueness check. Three coordinated changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Relaxed the `telephone` validation pattern from `^[0-9]*$` to `^[0-9 ()-]*$` so formatted input like `(613) 555-0100` passes DTO bean-validation instead of being rejected with a 400 before reaching the controller.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `normalizeTelephone(...)` helper that strips all non-digit characters. It's now applied:\n   - In `addOwner` right after mapping the DTO, so the **stored** value (and the value returned in the `telephone` field) is digits-only, and the uniqueness check runs against normalized numbers.\n   - Inside `ownerAlreadyExists`, replacing the previous generic whitespace-only `normalize`, so `(613) 555-0100` and `6135550100` collide.\n   - In `updateOwner`, for consistency on updates.\n\nThe entity's existing `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")` constraint is satisfied because normalization yields exactly 10 digits before persistence. Both new `Cp11Tests` (digits-only storage + normalized-duplicate rejection) pass, along with the full suite.",
